            <ArticleTitle>Bradyarrhythmic syncope in a patient with Prinzmetal's variant angina: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>996.e1-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ajem.2013.01.024</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0735-6757(13)00041-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a 46-year-old woman with Prinzmetal's angina and syncope due to severe bradyarrhythmias. Dynamic electrical changes were documented on 12-lead 24-hour electrocardiographic (ECG) monitoring. We highlight the importance of continuous ECG monitoring in making the diagnosis and the indication for permanent cardiac pacing in this case.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
